 ## Recovery response semantics
 
@@ -110,6 +111,17 @@ double-count shared work. If the SDK cannot expose a reliable value, omit it.
 Joined requests may include the shared records but have their own `trace_id`,
 `execution_time_ms`, and workflow output from their own replay.
 
+## Failure cooldown
+
+After a failed recovery the backend remembers that exact failure for 15 seconds. A request
+that fails the same way inside that window is answered from the memory instead of starting
+another agent run, so the agent is not re-run (and billed) for a failure it just could not fix.
+Such a response keeps the original `error` and `heal_records`, has its own `trace_id` and
+`execution_time_ms`, carries no `agent_cost_usd` or `agent_duration_ms`, and sets
+`cooldown_remaining_s` to the seconds left before a retry would start a fresh recovery.
+The field is omitted on every other response, including the failure that started the cooldown.
+Consumers can show "retry in N s" from it.
+
